1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,036
Imagine waking up tomorrow

2
00:00:02,036 --> 00:00:04,687
and finding out everyone in your city

3
00:00:04,687 --> 00:00:06,686
wants to take all their money out of the bank.

4
00:00:06,886 --> 00:00:07,761
What would happen?

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,024
Here's the secret.

6
00:00:11,224 --> 00:00:13,347
Banks don't keep every dollar you deposit

7
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:14,552
sitting in a vault.

8
00:00:14,752 --> 00:00:17,376
They use much of that money to make loans,

9
00:00:17,376 --> 00:00:19,659
like helping people buy homes and cars.

10
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:22,588
But what if everyone wanted their money back

11
00:00:22,588 --> 00:00:23,663
at the exact same time?

12
00:00:23,863 --> 00:00:25,773
The bank might not have enough cash ready

13
00:00:25,773 --> 00:00:27,532
to give everyone immediately!

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,387
This is called a bank run.

15
00:00:30,587 --> 00:00:33,173
If the bank has to sell things quickly to get cash,

16
00:00:33,173 --> 00:00:34,491
it could lose money.

17
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:36,419
And panic could spread to other banks!

18
00:00:36,839 --> 00:00:38,097
But here's the good news!

19
00:00:38,297 --> 00:00:42,834
In the United States, the FDIC protects eligible bank deposits

20
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:46,396
up to $250,000 per depositor,

21
00:00:46,396 --> 00:00:49,135
per insured bank, per ownership category.

22
00:00:49,555 --> 00:00:51,777
So banks work because not everyone

23
00:00:51,777 --> 00:00:53,309
needs all their money at once.

24
00:00:53,509 --> 00:00:55,856
That's why banks manage cash carefully

25
00:00:55,856 --> 00:00:57,115
and have safety systems.

26
00:00:57,315 --> 00:00:58,851
Would you keep your money in a bank?

